  "title": "Expulsion of the Peisistratid tyrants from Athens",
  "summary": "In 510 BCE the Spartan king Cleomenes I besieged the tyrant Hippias on the Acropolis and expelled him from Athens, after the exiled Cleisthenes had won Sparta's help. Power passed to the Athenian magistrates, and Cleisthenes later introduced reforms that gave power to the demos.",
